      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__PSA_1ga69aa2e5f10a1493bffeb51993ef4b09b" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int wolfSSL_set_psa_ctx</definition>
        <argsstring>(WOLFSSL *ssl, struct psa_ssl_ctx *ctx)</argsstring>
        <name>wolfSSL_set_psa_ctx</name>
        <param>
          <type>WOLFSSL *</type>
          <declname>ssl</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>struct psa_ssl_ctx *</type>
          <declname>ctx</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>与えられたSSLセッションのPSAコンテキストを設定する機能 </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function setup the PSA context for the given SSL session.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ssl</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>CTXが有効になるWolfSSLへのポインタ </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ctx</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Struct PSA_SSL_CTXへのポインタ（SSLセッションに固有である必要があります） </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>WOLFSSL_SUCCESS 成功した <emphasis>Example</emphasis> <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Create<sp/>new<sp/>ssl<sp/>session</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">WOLFSSL<sp/>*ssl;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">struct<sp/>psa_ssl_ctx<sp/>psa_ctx<sp/>=<sp/>{<sp/>0<sp/>};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ssl<sp/>=<sp/>wolfSSL_new(ctx);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">if<sp/>(!ssl)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>return<sp/>NULL;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>setup<sp/>PSA<sp/>context</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ret<sp/>=<sp/>wolfSSL_set_psa_ctx(ssl,<sp/>ctx);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__PSA_1ga49e96c7f54a0adeab54732a72291628c" kindref="member">wolfSSL_psa_set_private_key_id</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para>wolfSSL_psa_free_psa_ctx</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ssl</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>pointer to the WOLFSSL where the ctx will be enabled </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ctx</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>pointer to a struct psa_ssl_ctx (must be unique for a ssl session)</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>WOLFSSL_SUCCESS on success </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>BAD_FUNC_ARG if ssl or ctx are NULL</para>
</simplesect>
This function setup the PSA context for the TLS callbacks to the given SSL session. At the end of the session, the resources used by the context should be freed using <ref refid="group__PSA_1ga11022744c54e21738db6addde5064319" kindref="member">wolfSSL_free_psa_ctx()</ref>.</para>
<para><emphasis>Example</emphasis> <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Create<sp/>new<sp/>ssl<sp/>session</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">WOLFSSL<sp/>*ssl;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">struct<sp/>psa_ssl_ctx<sp/>psa_ctx<sp/>=<sp/>{<sp/>0<sp/>};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ssl<sp/>=<sp/>wolfSSL_new(ctx);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">if<sp/>(!ssl)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>return<sp/>NULL;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>setup<sp/>PSA<sp/>context</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ret<sp/>=<sp/>wolfSSL_set_psa_ctx(ssl,<sp/>ctx);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__PSA_1ga49e96c7f54a0adeab54732a72291628c" kindref="member">wolfSSL_psa_set_private_key_id</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para>wolfSSL_psa_free_psa_ctx </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
